msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[archers,†1]]1. Archers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:93
msgid ""
"High Elf archers add +1 to their dice roll when making Shooting attacks. "
"They will therefore score a hit against targets in the open on a 3 or more, "
"against targets that are defended on a 4 or more, and against fortified "
"targets on a 5 or more."
msgstr ""
"Les Archers Hauts Elfes rajoutent +1 lorsqu’elles lancent leurs dés pour "
"tirer : elles toucheront donc des cibles à découvert sur 3+, les cibles en "
"défense sur 4+ et les cibles fortifiées sur 5+."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[giant-eagles,†2]]2. Giant Eagles"
msgstr "[[giant-eagles,†2]]2. Aigles Géants"

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[dragons,†3]]3. Dragons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:99
msgid ""
"Dragons can fly. Dragon rider units and any other units that include a "
"Dragon riding character cause terror in their enemies."
msgstr ""
"Les Dragons peuvent voler. Les Chevaucheurs de Dragons et les unités "
"rejointes par un personnage monté sur un Dragon provoquent la terreur."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:110
msgid ""
"Because Dragon Riders have a great many hits (6) which are difficult to "
"inflict even during a lengthy combat engagement, we must consider the "
"possibility of hurting the Dragon and reducing its effectiveness in "
"subsequent turns. Therefore, if a Dragon Rider has accumulated 4–5 hits by "
"the end of the Shooting phase or Combat phase and is no longer engaged in "
"combat it is deemed to have been badly hurt. Once a Dragon has been badly "
"hurt all accumulated hits are discounted and its maximum hits value and "
"Attacks are halved for the rest of the battle (to 3 Hits and 3/2 Attacks)."
msgstr ""
"Un Chevaucheur de Dragon possède beaucoup de Points de Vie (6). Il serait "
"donc très difficile d’en venir à bout en un tour et, pour compenser cette "
"apparente invulnérabilité, la règle suivante s’applique : si un Chevaucheur "
"de Dragon a accumulé entre 4 et 5 touches à la fin d’une phase de Tir ou de "
"Combat, et qu'il n'est plus engagé, il est grièvement blessé. Une fois qu’un "
"Chevaucheur de Dragon est grièvement blessé, toutes les touches accumulées "
"jusque-là sont annulées mais ses Attaques et ses Points de Vie sont réduits "
"de moitié pour le reste de la partie (3/2 Attaques et 3 Points de Vie)."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:116
msgid ""
"Generals, Wizards and Heroes can ride Dragons. A Dragon can fly increasing "
"its rider’s move to 100cm. An extra [.edit]#+3/3# Attacks are added to those "
"of its rider. A Dragon can breathe fire if the character has joined a unit "
"that isn’t engaged in combat."
msgstr ""
"Les Généraux, Sorciers et Héros peuvent chevaucher des dragons. Un Dragon "
"peut voler, le mouvement du cavalier passe ainsi à 100 cm, et il ajoute "
"[.edit]#+3/3# Attaques à son cavalier. Un dragon chevauché par un personnage "
"ne peut cracher du feu que s’il a rejoint une unité qui n'est pas engagée au "
"corps-à-corps."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:123
msgid ""
"Dragons can make a fiery breath. This applies both to a unit of Dragon "
"Riders and to Dragons ridden by characters that have joined a unit of "
"troops. The fire breath has a range of 20cm. Breath can be directed against "
"one target as for normal shooting and has 3 Attacks that are worked out in "
"the usual way at 4+ to hit."
msgstr ""
"Les Dragons ont une attaque de tir spéciale : ils peuvent cracher du feu ! "
"Cela s’applique aux Chevaucheurs de Dragons aussi bien qu’aux Dragons "
"utilisés comme monture. Le souffle du Dragon fonctionne comme suit : le jet "
"de flammes a une portée de 20cm. Le Dragon peut choisir normalement sa cible "
"et lui inflige 3 Attaques de tir résolues de façon classique, touchant sur "
"4+."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[elven-bolt-thrower,†4]]4. Elven Bolt Thrower"
msgstr "[[elven-bolt-thrower,†4]]4. Baliste à Répétition"

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[wizard,†5]]5. Wizard"
msgstr "[[wizard,†5]]5. Sorcier"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:131
msgid ""
"High Elf Mages are especially powerful wizards and to represent this can re-"
"roll a failed spell on any dice result except a 1. If a spell is failed "
"because a 1 is rolled then no re-roll is permitted."
msgstr ""
"Les Mages Hauts Elfes sont de puissants sorciers. Pour représenter cela, en "
"cas d’échec, ils peuvent relancer le dé pour jeter un sort, à moins d’avoir "
"obtenu un 1. Si le sort est raté sur un 1, le dé ne peut pas être relancé."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:132
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[giant-eagle-mount,†6]]6. Giant Eagle Mount"
msgstr "[[giant-eagle-mount,†6]]6. Aigle Géant Monté"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:135
msgid ""
"Generals, Wizards and Heroes can ride a Giant Eagle. An Eagle can fly "
"increasing its rider’s move from 60 to 100cm. An extra +2 Attacks are added "
"to those of its rider."
msgstr ""
"Les Généraux, Sorciers et Héros peuvent monter des Aigles Géants. Les Aigles "
"Géants volent ; ils font donc passer le mouvement de leur cavalier de 60 à "
"100 cm, et lui ajoutent +2 Attaques."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:138
msgid ""
"Generals, Wizards and Heroes can ride Chariots. An extra +1 Attack is added "
"to those of its rider."
msgstr ""
"Un Général, un Sorcier ou un Héros peut combattre sur un Char. Le personnage "
"gagne alors +1 Attaque."

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "High Elf spells"
msgstr "Sorts Hauts Elfes"

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "Storm of Stone"
msgstr "Tempête de Pierres"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:151
msgid ""
"_The ground erupts around the Mage, and a hail of stones, rocks and dirt "
"hurls itself upon his foes._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:153
msgid "This spell affects every enemy unit within range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:160
msgid ""
"Every enemy unit within range takes 3 Attacks worked out in the normal way. "
"Unengaged units are not driven back by the Storm of Stone (the assault comes "
"from the ground beneath their feet). Engaged units carry over any hits "
"scored into the first round of combat; any hits scored count as having been "
"struck in the combat itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:162
#, no-wrap
msgid "Light of Battle"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:168
msgid ""
"_A radiant light shines forth upon the Mage’s companions filling them with "
"magical vigour._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:176
msgid ""
"The spell lasts for the duration of the following Combat phase.  Every unit "
"and every character that has joined a unit gains a bonus +1 attack. These "
"attacks can be allocated to any stand in the unit and can be allocated to a "
"different stand in each combat round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:178
#, no-wrap
msgid "Heaven’s Fire"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:184
msgid ""
"_The mage imbues the Elven archers with an unearthly swiftness enabling them "
"to rain death upon the enemy._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:189
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast upon a friendly unit of unengaged missile armed "
"infantry or cavalry within range. It cannot be cast on artillery. The Mage "
"does not need to be able to see the friendly unit nor their intended target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:195
msgid ""
"When the Heaven’s Fire spell is cast on a unit, it can shoot twice that turn "
"instead of once. If it has already shot that turn it can therefore shoot "
"again immediately. If it has yet to shoot it can shoot twice. When a unit "
"shoots twice due to Heaven’s Fire the second shot is always at a −1 penalty "
"to hit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:197
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hail of Destruction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:203
msgid ""
"_A hail of fiery arrows flies from the Mage’s outstretched finger tips and "
"strikes an enemy unit._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:207
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on an enemy unit. The Mage must be able to see his "
"target to use this spell. The spell cannot be directed at a unit engaged in "
"combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:212
msgid ""
"The Hail of Destruction is treated like three ordinary shooting attacks (4+ "
"to hit) except that armour has no effect (all targets count as having no "
"armour). A unit can be driven back by a Hail of Destruction as with ordinary "
"shooting."
msgstr ""
